WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:08.649 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  ahoy mateys  the countdown to rares March 20th  release of their swashbuckling pirate  game sea of thieves is officially  underway  and throughout the past few weeks we  dove into some of the titles latest  improvements during a studio visit and  various betas from pirate legends to  skeleton raids to the Kraken and beyond  here are 10 things we learned about  Microsoft's first exclusive title of  2018  [Music]  number one sailing the beautiful high  seas based on our experience with the  game thus far it's clear that rares  pirate adventure game is absolutely  gorgeous as the Sun sets and Rises on  the sea of Thieves rares use of Unreal  Engine 4 shines brightly aside from the  game's graphical quality its cartoon art  style complements the comedic and silly  aspects of the game like firing fellow  crewmates out of cannons or playing  pirate dress-up with Goofy accessories  sea of thieves art style is both  beautifully designed and humorously  quirky all at the same time number 2  thrilling pirate voyages voyages our sea  of thieves version of quests and you'll  need to visit an outpost to purchase a  voyage from one of the games three trade  companies the first faction is the gold  hoarders these gilded NPCs challenge you  to hunt for treasure via x marks the  spot maps and solving riddles the second  company is the order of souls these  mysterious NPCs will pay pirates to go  on bounty hunt for the most deadly  pirate captains the third and final  trade company that we know of is the  merchants alliance they will pay you to  scout for supplies like pigs chickens or  gunpowder across the sea the only caveat  is you must fulfill your contract on  time number three team up or go alone  it's no secret that sea of thieves is a  unique type of multiplayer game that  operates best when players adventure in  groups and communicate properly with one  another the larger galleon sailed by a  crew of four are not only better  equipped they are also more sturdy when  it comes to attacks yet if you prefer to  explore the world alone a single sailed  sloop is the perfect alternative these  small vessels are more nimble than  galleons but are far more fragile  everything necessary to operate the ship  including the sails wheel anchor and  math are within arm's reach even for  solo pirates number four guns at the  ready it's important to survey the seas  as danger lurks around every corner ship  the ship combat on the open ocean can be  chaos as the cannonballs whiz by you'll  need to juggle firing back  repairing holes and steering your vessel  while scouring the various islands on  foot you'll often run into other crews  your skeleton or its protecting their  treasures sword fights and gunplay can  be a little clunky but it's a pirate's  life for all and you'll need to fight  for your precious cargo number 5 dress  the part when you first fire up sea of  thieves you'll be greeted by the  infinite pirate generator you'll be able  to circle through eight pre-created  pirates coming in different shapes sizes  genders and appearances if none fit your  preference you can regenerate the eight  characters over and over again until you  find one you'd like to roleplay then at  outpost shops you can spend your  hard-earned gold on a ton of cosmetic  items to dress up your Buccaneer from  full costumes to peg legs how you choose  to outfit your character will allow you  to further standout rare has confirmed  that microtransactions will be in the  final game but stated there will not be  a loop box system nor will purchases  affect gameplay number 6 game-changing  treasures during the various Vedas  players discover two uniquely designed  chests with some interesting effects the  chest of a thousand rods will make the  carrier drunk immediately and the chest  of sorrow will periodically cry and fill  your ship with water if you don't bail  quickly these cursed chests are meant to  change the way you play the game and  although these chests might seem like an  unnecessary challenge they are worth  your trouble as they can be sold for far  more gold than  most regular chests rare has teased more  of these odd chests but we don't know  what effects they will have on the  player or the world around them  number seven skeleton forts since the  first sea of Thieves trailers launched  players have speculated about the scope  cloud with glowing green eyes we now  know it's one of the titles emergent  gameplay systems a giant skull cloud  will randomly appear above a particular  skeleton fort which informs all pirate  crews that a raid is going down as crews  converge on the island they can choose  to work together or battle each other  through the waves of enemies skeletons  once you've fought your way through the  Horde the captain will appear and  challenge you to a battle when the  captain is defeated the cloud will  dissipate and the skeleton will drop a  key to the fort's vault  once the vault is open other crews are  free to pillage  but how raids will transpire is up to  the players can crews work together or  will there be an all-out war for the  vault contents  [Music]  number eight become a pirate legend as  you level up your reputation with the  various factions you'll eventually be  approached by a mysterious group of NPCs  who you'll want to impress this is the  first form of endgame content once  you've proven your worth you'll be  invited into the tavern of Legends which  is hidden somewhere on the existing map  inside the secluded tavern the ghostly  pirate Lord will sell you legendary  voyages and although these voyages are  by far the most valuable in the game  they can still be shared with other  pirates regardless of their rank when  the first pirate legends arrive in the  hideout you'll begin to see some unique  cosmetic items and high ranking titles  sailing throughout the world  number 9 become a legendary captain for  the game's first major update rare has  planned yet another achievement to  strive towards becoming a legendary  captain the second tier of endgame  content makes the tavern of Legends your  personal hideout as you'll automatically  spawn there when signing on this ship  waiting in the background of the cave  will also become yours to sail and  customize when other players see the  legendary ships sail out for underneath  the hideouts waterfall imagine the  Batmobile bursting out of the back aged  they'll know a legendary captain is on  the Seas number 10 released the Kraken  finally we can confirm that the Kraken  patrols the oceans deep acting as a  force of nature similar to the game  storms that can emerge at any time  alongside details shared by rare we also  got our first glimpse at the monster  when screenshots leaked online this past  February the ocean will grow dark with  ink and the in-game music will begin to  change if the Beast draws near if you  are unable to outrun it the Kraken will  wrap its giant tentacles around your  ship and any other ships nearby  attempting to crush them beneath its  weight crew members can be attacked  thrown and thrashed around if you don't  bring the fight to its suction-cup  dilemma  there will be a reward if you and your  crew are able to take down the Kraken  but we will have to wait to find out  what that might be from the features  highlighted on this list - the  additional updates rare continues to  roll out see if thieves progression is  just getting started I for one am  excited to see what kind of Easter eggs  rare has in store for us as we scour the  Seas for remnants of banjo kazooie or  perfect dark so be sure to keep an eye  on gamespot.com for the latest sea of  thieves updates and our review later  this month  [Music]  [Music]

